cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Aionis in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Aionis: a falsifiable, anti-leakage quantitative-finance research harness"
authors:
  - name: The Aionis Authors
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rethymus/Aionis"
url: "https://rethymus.github.io/Aionis/"
abstract: >
  Aionis implements falsifiability as an engineering constraint for
  quantitative-finance research: one pre-registered two-tailed claim per phase
  on the cross-sectional monthly rank-IC of S&P 500 point-in-time constituents,
  with a config-before-result append-only ledger, purged group k-fold with
  embargo, pinned-version determinism, and honest null results with tight
  confidence intervals as the intended experimental outcome.
keywords:
  - quantitative-finance
  - point-in-time-data
  - preregistration
  - rank-ic
  - anti-leakage
  - research-integrity
